// expect: refuse E_TypeMismatch
// THE STAGE OF `each` ANSWERS `()`. An iteration-for-effect drops its stage's
// value by definition, so a stage that answers anything else is a value the
// program silently loses. Measured 2026-10-12 on boot 454c3aaf as a compiler
// defect this shape hid: a report call that had become a PARTIAL APPLICATION
// when its op grew a field — a function value — was handed to `each`, which
// discarded it, and every occurs-check refusal the graph's write guard noted
// vanished (`fn f(x) = x == [x]` checked clean). With the stage typed `()`
// the dropped value is a type error at the call. On main's tree through boot
// 454c3aaf this program compiled clean and ran to 0; the law lives in
// lib/prelude.mn, so the same boot over this tree's library refuses it.
fn main() = {
  each({ x => x + 1 }, [1, 2])
  0
}
